# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored and never leaves
# your machine, so nothing here reaches Netlify or GitHub.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_ prefix = CLIENT. Vite inlines these into the JS bundle at build time.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# That is the whole point of the prefix: Vite refuses to expose any other
# variable to browser code, so you cannot leak a server secret by accident.
# The flip side is that anything with the prefix IS public once deployed —
# on a live site it is readable straight out of the JS.
#
# So these are for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. Never set them on a host.
VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No prefix = SERVER. Only netlify/functions/ can read these.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set these in the Netlify dashboard, NOT here — this file is only a
# template, and the functions read them from the host's environment.
#
#   OPENAI_API_KEY   your key, used by the TTS proxy on behalf of invited
#                    users. Never sent to the browser.
#   ACCESS_TOKENS    comma-separated invite tokens, one per person, e.g.
#                    alice-7fq2,bob-p4xd. Empty means nobody gets in.
#
# See DEPLOY.md → "Sharing with friends".
